You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S05
Scenario title: Specification Document Review
Initial workflow description:
An engineer reviews a specification document to check whether new features are reflected correctly and whether there are typos or missing details.

Domain expert answers:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What event or condition triggers the start of a document review — for example, is it a document submission notification, a scheduled milestone, or an ad-hoc request from a colleague?",
      "answer": "The review begins when the document reviewer collects the specification document along with the related feature change list. The specific triggering event (e.g., submission notification, milestone, or ad-hoc request) is not specified in the workflow."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "Does the engineer follow a defined checklist or set of criteria when reviewing the document, or is the review based on personal expertise and judgment?",
      "answer": "The reviewer uses a defined review checklist as an input to the process. The review covers feature coverage against a change list, as well as terminology and formatting consistency — indicating structured, criteria-based review rather than purely personal judgment."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "In what format are the specification documents provided, and in which system or tool are they stored and accessed during the review?",
      "answer": "Documents are accessed via a document repository. A commenting tool is also used during review. The specific file format of the specification documents is not specified in the workflow."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "What are the possible outcomes at the end of a review, and what happens next in each case — for example, who is notified and what action is expected from them?",
      "answer": "Two outcomes are possible: (1) all feature changes are reflected — the document proceeds toward approval; (2) changes are missing — the document author revises it based on recorded comments. After revision, the feature owner confirms changes, and the approver makes a final approval decision or requests another revision."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "Are there other roles involved in the review process beyond the engineer, such as a second reviewer, a team lead who must approve, or an author who must respond to findings?",
      "answer": "Yes. Beyond the document reviewer, three other roles are involved: the document author (who revises the document based on comments), the feature owner (who confirms revisions), and the approver (who makes the final approval decision)."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "Approximately how many specification documents does the engineer review per week or month, and how long does a typical review take from start to finish?",
      "answer": "The workflow does not specify the volume of documents reviewed per week or month, nor the typical duration of a review from start to finish."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Incorporate the answers and produce an updated structured workflow representation plus automation opportunities.
Record unknown facts as remaining gaps, rather than asserting unsupported details.
Return JSON with this shape:
